    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Stoddard is notable as one of the few communities along the Mississippi River that was never a trading post or riverboat stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoddard%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The construction of Lock and Dam Number Eight in 1937 flooded the lowlands, literally bringing the river to the town of Stoddard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoddard%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Stoddard Historic District features well-preserved nineteenth-century buildings, including the village's old schoolhouse and post office.",
